# VIGIL SaaS money-IN drain — config for vigil-billing-drain.service   (MONEY path)
# Copy to ~/.config/vigil/billing-drain.env with mode 0600 (`install -m 600 …`). PREFER systemd credentials for
# the secrets below (GO-LIVE §9: never in the repo, avoid a plaintext env var at rest): a drop-in with
# `LoadCredential=<NAME>:<file>` (or `LoadCredentialEncrypted=`), which the drain reads itself from
# $CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY/<NAME> — see vigil-billing-drain.service — so the secret is never in the unit-wide
# environment. Setting them HERE is the documented FALLBACK (a credential of the same name wins). NEVER commit it.
# ONE DRAINER: use the vigil-billing-drain TIMER or a manual `sigil billing-drain watch` — never both.
# =====================================================================
# Paths in THIS file must be ABSOLUTE (systemd does NOT expand %h inside an EnvironmentFile value; the CLI
# refuses a relative / %-bearing spool). With none set, the drain derives the spool from SIGIL_HOME (below).

# REQUIRED to run at all (the drain is DEFAULT-OFF and refuses without it). Also set it in
# ~/.config/vigil/alerts.env so `vigil alerts` watches this unit fail-closed from the start.
# VIGIL_BILLING_DRAIN_ENABLED=1

# REQUIRED: the Flutterwave webhook verif-hash secret (the SAME value the proxy's /webhooks/billing route uses).
# VIGIL_BILLING_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# REQUIRED: the processor secret key for the MANDATORY server-side transaction re-verify (without it the drain
# refuses — a verif-hash alone never grants value). Owner-provisioned; never paste it anywhere but here or a
# credential file.
# VIGIL_FLW_SECRET_KEY=

# REQUIRED IF YOU MOVED SIGIL_HOME (GO-LIVE §2): the same value the cockpit uses. The drain mints onto the spine
# under it and, with nothing else set, drains $SIGIL_HOME/billing-spool (the GO-LIVE runbook path). Forget it and
# the drain finds no owner identity under ~/.sigil and REFUSES (the unit goes FAILED) — never a "healthy" no-op.
# SIGIL_HOME=/mnt/vigil-data/.sigil

# OPTIONAL: copy the proxy's VIGIL_BILLING_WEBHOOK_SPOOL here (where /webhooks/billing writes) if it is NOT
# $SIGIL_HOME/billing-spool — the drain then drains exactly that directory.
# VIGIL_BILLING_WEBHOOK_SPOOL=/mnt/vigil-data/.sigil/billing-spool

# OPTIONAL (legacy override): an explicit spool to drain. It MUST equal the proxy's VIGIL_BILLING_WEBHOOK_SPOOL —
# the drain refuses (the unit goes FAILED) when the two are both set and differ, or when this is
# ~/.sigil/billing-spool while SIGIL_HOME points elsewhere. Prefer leaving it unset.
# VIGIL_BILLING_SPOOL=/home/USER/.sigil/billing-spool

# OPTIONAL (NET-2b, default OFF): auto-retry a webhook whose processor re-verify hit a TRANSIENT failure (timeout,
# connection reset, HTTP 408/425/429/5xx) instead of quarantining it on sight. It is parked in <spool>/retry/ and
# re-tried on a bounded schedule (5 s doubling to 5 min, at most 8 retries ≈ 15 min); if the processor is still
# failing after that it is quarantined and this unit alarms exactly as without the flag. Nothing is ever minted
# without a successful re-verify, and a retry cannot double-credit (sha256 dedup + event_id idempotency).
# VIGIL_NET_RECOVERY_ENABLED=1
